What do the observations actually determine? (@ql-identifiability: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @quantitative-literacy, #source @ql-source-insight, #source @ql-source-algebra, #source @ql-source-uncertainty, #quantitative-literacy "../study/Reading-a-technical-claim.lingua#r_2QQHDYD4PQCPQ2CQY3BC53MHP9", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../../../physics/thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/measurement/Inverse-thermal-problems-identifiability-and-regularization.lingua#r_5N261RJHPXAZ52AG7TC3Y5CW7H", #fluid-dynamics "../../../physics/fluid-dynamics/measurement/Infer-flow-properties-with-identifiability-and-independent-data.lingua#r_3N09ZV623SWF4TRBTXH6AYY085") { r_5J7K2N4XB97BQSJBCXCMCJVC5W
**Read:** The Art of Insight, Abstraction, Probabilistic reasoning, and Easy cases; Algebra and Trigonometry 2e's linear-model and systems sections. Revisit the measurement vocabulary and the NIST guide's discussion of measurement models.

A fitted model and its parameter values are claims about a relation within conditions. Observing y = ax + b at a single x gives one constraint on two unknowns. Repeating that same x more precisely does not identify a and b separately. Two different inputs can identify the ideal two-parameter linear relation algebraically, but do not test its linearity over an interval.

Parameter identifiability, statistical uncertainty, and physical validity are different questions. A model can fit all observations while omitting a mechanism, or have several parameter combinations that produce indistinguishable outputs. A hidden change in sample basis can imitate a process improvement. Conversely, a poor numerical fit may result from a transcription error rather than a new physical law.

**Work:** use teaching readings (0,0.2), (50,2.2), and (100,4.2) in stated units. Fit a linear relation, reverse it where possible, and identify what the middle point tests. Replace that middle output by 2.5 and compare a model discrepancy, an input error, and a changed experimental condition as hypotheses. State an observation that would distinguish them.

For a material balance, count independent constraints and unknown streams before solving. Explain whether one additional flow reading or one composition reading would answer the actual question. Preserve a prediction on an observation not used to choose the model. A perfect residual is evidence of agreement with these data, not proof of a unique mechanism or a universal engineering law.

